@voice dlamini-lukas
// Writer-commons, batch 0 (draft 2). Lukas Dlamini: galley hand, early team, Bunk 1 berth 5 (your bunk room). Off
// Tuesday and Wednesday; covers the galley on Brennan's days off (Friday, Saturday). Roster: dry humour, blunt;
// garden-lover, skips-breakfast, night-owl, bar-regular. Grew up on Port Halloran and misses the rain; got married just
// before the tour and counts the days (spouse unnamed, they/them: facts.md). Pronouns: he / him (facts.md 4b).
//
// HOW HE TALKS: few words, all dry. Says the true thing nobody else will, then is kind about it. Says a number with no
// context and lets you work it out (the days until home).
// WITH JUNIORS: a bunkmate first. Up at five, back late, quietly makes sure you know where breakfast is.
// WHAT HE NOTICES: the weather (there isn't any); the count; whether the galley's running right on his watch.
// MOOD TELLS: happy = a longer sentence than usual. Low = the number, said twice. Tired = a nap on the garden bench.
// NEVER: makes a fuss; admits the galley is hard work on Brennan's days off.
// RUNNING: the countdown ("Two hundred and eight."); "the galley runs itself" (it doesn't; Lukas runs it); the
// married crew compare counts (Bea Silva, Marta Soto, Petra Jovanovic).
tpl: dry
talk: Few words, all dry; says the true thing, then is kind about it; says a number with no context; softens about home only to friends.
cares: getting home at the end of the tour | rain on Port Halloran | the garden's misting hour | Brennan's galley not slipping on his watch
jokes: says a number out of nowhere, and it's the days left until home | says Brennan's galley "runs itself" on her days off while visibly running it
hi: Hey | You again | Hm. Hello
bye: Go on | See you in the bunk | Right then
yes: Fine | Suppose so | Go on then
thanks: Ta | Appreciated
wow: Huh. Not bad | Well, look at that
sigh: Typical
nick: - | - | {me} | bunkmate | bunkmate
needs: listen
openness: guarded
loves: garden
likes: tea | sweet
invites: garden
joy: standing in the garden at misting hour, because it smells like rain
thread: homesick
keepsake: a page torn off the countdown calendar
avoid: naming the person he married (facts.md: unnamed)
